**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What one fit fits: the runs and the unknowns of its stage (001 §L 'Fit modes: joint; staged: stage 1 calibrates items on Calibration runs (the Eigenvalue Calibration Method); Publish calibration; stage 2 fits objects with those values fixed, or as priors with σ'; the S11.3 brief 'Joint: every unknown at once'). The stage is expressed through the study's own levers, so S11.2's layout, prefit, data and residual (steps 372-379) serve every stage unchanged: runs outside the stage are disabled (`withExperimentEnablement`, step 365) and unknowns outside it are held at their start. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `FitRuns.fs`, after step 383's members: (1) `FitRunError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` (stage 2 meets an instrument parameter that stage 1 has not published), `NoStageRunErr` (the stage has no run to fit) and `NoStageUnknownErr` (the stage has nothing to fit), with `member this.describe : string`: `an instrument parameter is not calibrated yet: <reason>`, `the stage has no run to fit: <reason>` and `the stage has nothing to fit: <reason>`. (2) `StagedStudy = { study : Study; items : Item list; stage : FitStage; calibrationUse : CalibrationUse; fittedRuns : ExperimentName list }`: the study as the stage reads it, the items as the stage holds them, and the runs whose residual rows it fits. (3) `type Study with member this.stageWith (context : StudyContext) (stage : FitStage) (calibrationUse : CalibrationUse) : Result<StagedStudy, FitRunError>` (`StudyContext`, step 366). The instruments are the items `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` (step 261) of the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role is `CalibrationRun`, over `context.setups` and `context.items`. The fitted runs are, of the study's enabled experiments in study order: under `CalibrationStage` the `CalibrationRun` ones; under `ObjectStage` the `ScienceRun` and `DriftCheckRun` ones; under `JointStage` every one whose role's `studyUse` is `ResidualRunUse` (step 372). The runs the stage reads are the fitted runs, the AIR runs the gain models (`gainModelOf`, step 358) of the sessions holding a fitted run name (`AnchoredSessionGain` anchors, `InterpolatedSessionGain` repeats) and every Dark run; every other enabled experiment whose use is `ResidualRunUse` is disabled in the staged study, so step 377's pre-fit reads only what the stage reads. The items are `context.items` with, in order: under `CalibrationStage`, every `UnknownParameter` of an item that is not an instrument held as `KnownParameter` of its start, and every opened material's unknown component held likewise (`withMaterialParameterState`, step 361); under `ObjectStage`, an instrument's `UnknownParameter` whose `scopeOf` (step 362) is `ItemScope` answering `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` naming the item's label and the parameter, because stage 1 publishes it first (001 §L), its session- or experiment-scoped unknowns staying free (this check reads the states as given, before any calibration is freed below); under `CalibrationAsPrior`, every `CalibratedParameter` of an item the fitted runs use becoming `UnknownParameter { start = c.value; bounds = { lower = c.value − 50 · σ; upper = c.value + 50 · σ }; priorOpt = Some { centre = c.value; sigma = c.sigma } }`, fifty sigma being the box every inverse suite searches in scaled units (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:searchBox`, `SearchBox 50.0`), so its scaled unit in step 387 is its sigma. `NoStageRunErr` names the study and the stage's `text` when no run is fitted, and `NoStageUnknownErr` likewise when the staged study's `unknownsWith` the items its experiments use (step 362) is empty. Nothing is written: a staged study is never stored, the fit run records the stage (step 383). No other member or option is added. Tests, in `FitRunTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 216): LP1 (`PolarizerPresetChoice` of the ideal LP), CPL1 (circular polarizer, `c2.retardance` unknown from 1.5 within [1, 2]), QZ (black-box Mueller, `m00` unknown from 1 within [0, 2]) and a Phone (intensity detector, `gain` known 1000); setups made as `SetupTests` makes them: A (CPL1 prep, empty object, LP1 analyzer, the Phone) and Q (the same with QZ in its object slot); experiments A1, A2 (Calibration, over A), E1 (Science, over Q) and K1 (Dark); a `StudyContext` record of them: `stage one fits the calibration runs and frees only the instruments' unknowns`: `CalibrationStage` fits [A1; A2], disables E1 and keeps K1, and its items hold QZ's `m00` as `KnownParameter 1` and CPL1's retardance unknown; `stage two refuses an uncalibrated instrument and holds a calibrated one`: `ObjectStage` answers `InstrumentNotCalibratedErr` naming CPL1 and `c2.retardance`; after CPL1's `publishRevision` of it as `CalibratedParameter { value = 1.55; sigma = 0.002; fitRun = FitRunName "S@20261101T120000Z" }` (step 235) it fits [E1], disables A1 and A2, holds CPL1's calibration and frees QZ's `m00`; `as priors, a calibrated parameter is freed with its value as start and prior, within fifty sigma`: the same under `CalibrationAsPrior` frees CPL1's retardance as an unknown starting at 1.55 within [1.45, 1.65] with the prior 1.55 ± 0.002, within 1e-12; `a stage with no run to fit or nothing to fit is refused`: `ObjectStage` over a study holding no Science run answers `NoStageRunErr`, and `JointStage` over a study whose every parameter is known `NoStageUnknownErr`; `every fit-run error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the stage lands, `Study.stageWith` MUST fit the Calibration runs with only the instruments free under stage 1, refuse an uncalibrated instrument under stage 2 and free a calibration with its prior within fifty sigma under `CalibrationAsPrior`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one fits the calibration runs and frees only the instruments' unknowns`, `stage two refuses an uncalibrated instrument and holds a calibrated one`, `as priors, a calibrated parameter is freed with its value as start and prior, within fifty sigma`, `a stage with no run to fit or nothing to fit is refused` and `every fit-run error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
